      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting alloy has a hierarchical microstructure of dual-phase lamellar colonies.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6478865::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC7516913::web::025::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lamellar microstructure consists of fcc and B2 phases, with bcc nanoscale precipitates in the B2 lamellae.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6478865::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC7516913::web::025::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The untreated alloy has approximately 8% room-temperature tensile ductility.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocations accumulate or pile up near internal lamellar interfaces during deformation.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6478865::web::030::conclusions_and_summary"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation pile-ups at internal lamellar boundaries produce stress concentrations, microcracking, and limited ductility.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A first aging stage at about 580 °C for 1–2 hours will nucleate L12 precipitates uniformly.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6478865::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC7516913::web::025::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A subsequent hold at about 600 °C for 2–4 hours will cause preferential coarsening and migration of L12 precipitates toward internal lamellar boundaries.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Low-temperature aging of Al0.7CoCrFeNi can form coherent nanoscale L12 precipitates in the fcc lamellae.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6478865::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC6478865::web::030::conclusions_and_summary",
        "PMC7516913::web::025::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed treatment will preferentially localize L12 precipitates along fcc/B2 lamellar boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boundary-localized L12 precipitates will act as dislocation sinks.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitates will absorb or redistribute dislocations and thereby disrupt dislocation accumulation at internal interfaces.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced interfacial dislocation accumulation will lower local stress concentrations and suppress microcrack nucleation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Suppressing local stress concentrations and microcrack nucleation will improve strain accommodation and work hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treated alloy will retain or increase its yield strength relative to the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6478865::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC6478865::web::030::conclusions_and_summary",
        "PMC7516913::web::025::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treated alloy will have a yield strength of approximately 1074–1100 MPa or more.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will increase room-temperature tensile ductility from approximately 8% to about 15–20%.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed benefits are expected under room-temperature quasi-static tensile loading at a strain rate near 10^-3 s^-1.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
